CM_ BO_ 1568 "Two-step 100 Hz sync. CM5 sends the actual hardware transmit SOF timestamp of a previous sync. Nodes match PreviousSequence to a hardware receive SOF; timestamps use 0.1 ms ticks modulo 65536. A DBC does not implement the synchronization.";
CM_ SG_ 1568 PreviousTxTimestamp "Actual leader transmit SOF time of PreviousSequence in 0.1 ms ticks; wraps every 6553.6 ms. Ignore when PreviousTimestampValid is invalid.";
CM_ SG_ 1568 PreviousTimestampValid "Valid only when the preceding transmit SOF timestamp was captured; 0 at startup or capture failure.";
CM_ SG_ 1568 PreviousSequence "Sequence identifying the frame whose transmit SOF is reported.";
CM_ SG_ 1568 Sequence "Sequence number of this sync frame; wraps modulo 256.";
CM_ BO_ 1584 "Four consecutive samples per axis at 208 Hz; one frame per four samples is 52 Hz (19.2308 ms). DBC 19 ms is a nominal integer-millisecond estimate. Timestamp identifies sample 1; timestamp uses 0.1 ms ticks modulo 65536.";
CM_ SG_ 1584 AccelerationZ4 "Chronological sample 4 of AccelerationZ; indices 1..4 align across axes within this batch. Physical unit g.";
